From e05f804be1008890062dd1b3fc0109bac8360575 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:02:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper: preamble puncturing, front-chain narrowness, add-on
 anchors

- Static preamble puncturing: per-radio wlN_punct setting on Wireless >
  Settings, applied live through `wl eht dissubchan` by the one-shot
  applier rc/reaper_punct.c (boot, wireless start, page apply, rwatch
  tick); state in /tmp/reaper_punct.state.
- Dynamic preamble puncturing: new rpunctd controller (timed chanim_stats
  windows, hold/gain/interval gates, presets, optional confirmation
  scan, blacklist and fallback); runs only while a radio is Dynamic.
  Wireless Quality card and a Settings status line. The controller's
  file mirrors its belief and is reconciled by the rwatch tick.
- Front chains: the narrowness patterns hook.sh and rwatch 3d use come
  from rc/reaper_hook.h; in FORWARD only a destination counts as narrow,
  a RETURN inside a user chain is not a bypass.
- Rule Status "Re-check now" runs reaper_fwsim in a detached worker
  instead of inside httpd.
- Add-on installers (Skynet, MerlinAU, YazFi): the retired stock menu
  lines return as hidden anchors; pages inserted beside them land in
  Addons.
- Diagnostics v1.3.22/v1.3.23: puncturing, Dual WAN block, log-level
  finding, hardware block (SoC, clocks, board ID, switch, radios).
- wlcsm_bindfix default removed; daemon build outputs git-ignored.
- 39 dictionary tokens in all 25 packs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
